config BR2_PACKAGE_SPLASH
	bool "splash (framebuffer boot splash)"
	select BR2_PACKAGE_FIGLET
	help
	  Draw the openHC banner directly on /dev/fb0 at boot: green on
	  black, centred, no text console involved.

	  The banner is generated on the device by figlet at boot, so it
	  is not frozen into the image. figlet slant uses only the five characters
	  ". / \ _" and space, so splash draws them as strokes rather
	  than carrying a font or a bitmap. Change the word, get a new
	  picture, at whatever size the panel is.

	  Needs a 32bpp framebuffer. On the EA boards that is ce5300-fb,
	  which hands over the scanout CEFDK leaves running.
